        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n3. The trial Court vide order dated 20.09.2024 had permitted the petitioner to place on record the certified copy of the reply / written statement in the case titled as \"Rakesh Kumar vs. Subhash Chand\" by observing that the copy of the pet"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "d90837adbf3e4505ab097a6dd8049e21_16",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "6. The right to produce additional evidence was provided under Order 18 Rule 17A in the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908 and the said provision read as \"Production of evidence not previously known or which could not be produced despite due dil"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "5c891b00cd3d4edf95b0bae5a8e9ecf1_17",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "There is no provision in the Code of Civil Procedure that gives a right to the party to lead additional evidence."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "206551541d29411dbc3ba36c200629f0_20",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the present case, it is not in dispute that the entire evidence of the petitioner as well as of the respondent-landlord 3 of 5 Neutral Citation No:=2024:PHHC:131756 has been concluded and thus,\nthere is no right vested in the petitioner "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "ea324db082e74ac08de04f2968c74305_21",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "7. In addition to the same, it would be also relevant to note that the complaint dated 03.09.2018 is not relevant for the purpose of adjudication of the eviction proceedings."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "edfbd3fd351a481c818ecccba4e18de2_22",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "On a pointed query raised by this Court, learned counsel for the petitioner has not been able to refer any averment in the said complaint dated 03.09.2018 which shows that the respondent is the exclusive owner of the premises in question."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "ae64d869578847bb987b9405a5db1c78_23",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Merely because the respondent is shown to be a food business operator does not mean that it is the respondent, who is the owner of the property."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "6a9b553a70c1402d8a3dad5495dcd030_24",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Moreover, there are specific pleadings in paragraph 4(ii) of the eviction petition in which it has been specifically stated by the respondent herein that he is working with his brother in the shop under the name and style of M/s Jain Mistha"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "065a7c12eb454b55b384198a71fecf6b_25",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The complaint also pertains to M/s Jain Misthan Bhandar in which the respondent is stated to be a food business operator and the said aspect of the respondent working in the said premises has already been stated by the respondent-landlord i"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "bd759cfba7924955a5a13eba8ddb725c_26",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It cannot be inferred from the complaint dated 03.09.2018 that the sole proprietor of the said M/s Jain Mishtan Bhandar is the respondent and not his brother Subhash Chander Jain."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "2255748ce9044e3aad9939c766594802_27",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nIt would also be relevant to note that the said complaint dated 03.09.2018 was in existence much prior to the filing of the eviction petition in the year 2020 and also prior to the petitioner leading his evidence."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "f71467ae99cd4363a5c2a2dcf1a3f09b_29",
        "summary_section": "decision",
